    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q10a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x-3}{x-4}=\\dfrac{x+12}{x+8}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=8$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne4,-8$. Multiply both sides by $(x-4)(x+8)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-3)(x+8)&=(x+12)(x-4)\\\\x^2+5x-24&=x^2+8x-48\\\\24&=3x\\\\x&=8\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is permitted by the original denominators.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q10b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x}{x-3}+\\dfrac{2}{x-5}=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{21}{5}$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne3,5$. Multiply through by $(x-3)(x-5)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x-5)+2(x-3)&=(x-3)(x-5)\\\\x^2-5x+2x-6&=x^2-8x+15\\\\-3x-6&=-8x+15\\\\5x&=21\\\\x&=\\frac{21}{5}\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is permitted by the original denominators.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q10c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x+2}{x-3}+\\dfrac{x+2}{x-6}=2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{54}{13}$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne3,6$. Multiply through by $(x-3)(x-6)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+2)(x-6)+(x+2)(x-3)&=2(x-3)(x-6)\\\\x^2-4x-12+x^2-x-6&=2x^2-18x+36\\\\2x^2-5x-18&=2x^2-18x+36\\\\13x&=54\\\\x&=\\frac{54}{13}\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is permitted by the original denominators.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q10d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3x+2}{x-1}+\\dfrac{2x-4}{x+2}=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=6$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne1,-2$. Multiply through by $(x-1)(x+2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(3x+2)(x+2)+(2x-4)(x-1)&=5(x-1)(x+2)\\\\3x^2+8x+4+2x^2-6x+4&=5x^2+5x-10\\\\5x^2+2x+8&=5x^2+5x-10\\\\18&=3x\\\\x&=6\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is permitted by the original denominators.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q10e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x+1}-\\dfrac{2}{x+2}+\\dfrac{1}{x+4}=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne-1,-2,-4$. Multiply through by $(x+1)(x+2)(x+4)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+2)(x+4)-2(x+1)(x+4)+(x+1)(x+2)&=0\\\\x^2+6x+8-2x^2-10x-8+x^2+3x+2&=0\\\\-x+2&=0\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is permitted by the original denominators.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q10f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3x}{x-1}-\\dfrac{2x}{2x-1}=2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{2}{5}$",
          "worked": "$x\\ne1,\\frac12$. Multiply through by $(x-1)(2x-1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x(2x-1)-2x(x-1)&=2(x-1)(2x-1)\\\\6x^2-3x-2x^2+2x&=4x^2-6x+2\\\\4x^2-x&=4x^2-6x+2\\\\5x&=2\\\\x&=\\frac25\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is permitted by the original denominators.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      }
    ]
